# Project Development Conventions

## Imports

- Use the path alias `@` to point to the `src` directory
- Use the path alias `@@` to point to the `src/common` directory

## Coding

- Write clean, non-redundant, and readable code; always extract shared logic
- Write developer-friendly comments for key steps and methods
- Code must be able to run immediately, including all necessary imports and dependencies
- Avoid JS and CSS syntax with poor compatibility; provide corresponding comments when using it
- Prefer referencing the coding style of existing project code
- Prefer using the project's built-in components and utilities, then the already introduced third-party dependencies; avoid reinventing the wheel
- Avoid hardcoding and magic strings

## Code Checking

- Use ESLint for code linting and formatting
- Disable Prettier for code formatting

## Local Environment

- Use node version 20.19+ or 22.12+ or the latest stable version
- Use pnpm 10+ or the latest stable version as the package manager
